Package: MAC.address
Title: Find, Validate and Identify Device MAC Addresses
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Enrique", "Pérez Herrero",
    email = "eph.project1500@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools to work with MAC (Media Access Control) addresses: list the
    MAC addresses of the local network interfaces and of the neighbors in the
    ARP cache on Linux, macOS and Windows, extract MAC addresses from free
    text, validate and normalize their notation, check the multicast and
    locally administered bits, generate random addresses, derive IPv6
    interface identifiers (modified EUI-64), and identify the manufacturer using the public IEEE (Institute of
    Electrical and Electronics Engineers) MA-L, MA-M and MA-S registries
    <https://regauth.standards.ieee.org/standards-ra-web/pub/view.html#registries>.
URL: https://github.com/EnriquePH/mac-address,
    https://enriqueph.github.io/mac-address/
BugReports: https://github.com/EnriquePH/mac-address/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports:
    stats,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    curl,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
